The AI text: what was right and wrong
Right:
a quadratic Bézier is an exact parabola;
degree elevation preserves it;
the 2/3 rule from the anchor toward the tangent intersection is correct;
the first 4/3 configuration in the chat is valid.
Wrong:
For y=x² on [−3,3], the quadratic controls are (−3,9), (0,−9), (3,9), so the elevated cubic is (−3,9), (−1,−3), (1,−3), (3,9). The chat’s (−1,3), (1,3) is off by the sign of the handles.
The tangent slope at x=−3 is −6, not −3.
The claimed 3/4 configuration has slopes ±9/8, not ±3/4, and its handle length is not an integer.
“72,000 factors as 98,000” is nonsense; 72,000 = 2⁶ · 3² · 5³.
The 1/9 denominator is 27, not 9³; the “729” explanation is wrong.
The internal control points are not generally collinear; each lies on its own tangent line toward Q.
Grid decision
I went with 360,000 as the default large grid, as you suggested. It covers halves, quarters, eighths and twenty-fifths. Ninths require another ×27; if both 1/9 and 1/25 must stay exact, the common scale is 9,720,000. The 27 multiplier is not the default.

